WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:05.738 line:0%
-♪ Drop it in, drop it in,
d-d-d-drop it in ♪

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:07.807 line:0%
♪ Yeah ♪
-Dalvin, you're named

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.310 line:0%
NFC Offensive
Player of the Week today.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:11.777 line:0%
How do you feel about that?

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:15.648 line:0%
-Great. Um, give all the credit
to the O line up front,

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:17.217 line:0%
receivers, tight ends,

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:19.519 line:0%
just going out there
and just working hard.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:23.789 line:0%
And I run yards like Swiss
chard, so that's what it is.

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:26.593 line:0%
-What is your favorite part
about being a receiver?

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:29.495 line:0%
Is it catching touchdown passes?
Is it your dance celebrations?

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:32.432 line:0%
-Uh, I believe catching
the touchdown passes,

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.333 line:0%
'cause, you know,
they're like Pokémon to me.

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:36.269 line:0%
I got to have them all.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.604 line:0%
-What makes that connection
with you guys

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:42.208 line:0%
on that particular throw so
difficult for anybody to defend?

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.777 line:0%
-Yeah, I mean, it's like
a saying my mom used to say.

00:00:44.777 --> 00:00:49.382 line:0%
"It must be maple syrup, because
butter don't drizzle like that."

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.751 line:0%
-Ryan, do you stick with
the finger-roll celebration

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.252 line:0%
or do you change it up?
-You know,

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:54.553 line:0%
I think I got to stick with it.

00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:57.623 line:0%
You know, I think through
the whole process I learned

00:00:57.623 --> 00:01:00.626 line:0%
that's why you call them
touchdowns and not touch-ups.

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:03.596 line:0%
-But again, I mean, myself, you
know, I'm looking forward to it.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:07.000 line:0%
You know, again, you know,
call me Old Fashioned.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.201 line:0%
You know, like, literally.
I mean it.

00:01:09.201 --> 00:01:11.370 line:0%
Call me Old Fashioned.
That's my new nickname.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.239 line:0%
-I mean, you know,
on the team right now,

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.341 line:0%
they call me Old Fashioned.
You know, I mean it.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.810 line:0%
You know, that's my new
nickname, Old Fashioned.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.779 line:0%
-Maybe even I'll bring that up

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.748 line:0%
and put that in his ear
a little bit.

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:27.587 line:0%
You know, sometimes you got to
throw the sauce at your boss.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.289 line:0%
-Well, you know,
there's not a week that goes by

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:32.758 line:0%
where Coach Reid
isn't gonna on you, man.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:34.460 line:0%
That's his job, you know?

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.628 line:0%
Sometimes
you just got to be like,

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.163 line:0%
"Take it easy,
RollerCoaster Tycoon."

00:01:38.163 --> 00:01:39.264 line:0%
You know what I mean?

00:01:39.264 --> 00:01:40.533
-What you mom said is

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.535
a quote that
I am not familiar with.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:43.970
Can you elaborate
a little more on that?

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.205
-Syrup drizzles.
You got to make that play.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.841
Uh, a stick of butter --
it's a block.

00:01:48.841 --> 00:01:51.910
You got to put that
in the microwave to melt it.

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:53.346
That just takes too long.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.248
You got to make
that play right away, baby,

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:58.851
and that's why, you know, that's
why I'm like the maple syrup.

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:00.853
That's why she used to
always say that

00:02:00.853 --> 00:02:02.288
'cause I'm quick with it.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.624
I just drizzle
all over the place.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.626
[ Chuckles ]
-Thank you so much.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.894
-No problem. Thank you.

